      "content": "According to HACCP guidelines, cooked, ready-to-eat poultry must be cooled from an internal temperature of at least 165°F (74°C) to 40°F (4°C) within 2 hours, with dishes cooled to 40°F (4°C) or below within 4 hours. You should also consider the \"2-hour rule\" for dishes kept below 70°F (21°C). This will help minimize the risk of Clostridium perfringens growth.",
